You can turn on DECGraphics or IBMGraphics, depending on what client
you're using, and they'll improve the text mode slightly.  If you're on
Windows, use PuTTY, set the character set to CP437, and turn on
IBMGraphics.  If you're on a *nix, usually just turning on DECGraphics
will work fine, and I personally use the built-in telnet for *nix
because it's actually a proper implementation and about as 'lightweight'
as it gets.  :)  For Windows, PuTTY is excellent.

